# The agents' role documents. These are internal instruction bundles, not
# documentation: each one names a third party's infrastructure and account
# details (a school's self-hosted Forgejo instance and the classmate who owns
# the repos, the commercial messaging account whose keys send real mail), and
# each one tells the reader exactly which file on the box holds the live
# credential for it. They also carry the standing operational risk notes —
# which units must not be restarted, which key is not a sandbox. None of that
# survives publication, and this repo is public.
#
# The bundles live on the box under ~/.paperclip and are deployed there by
# hand. This rule is the only thing keeping them out of the repo; publishing
# them is a decision, not a cleanup. Path-scoped on purpose — it must not
# swallow an unrelated `onboarding/` somewhere else under agents/.
paperclip-bridge/onboarding/
